+/*
+ * z63-still-capture (off by default; for use with ../z9-qemu's capture
+ * models, the D980 writer among them). A release on this image drives
+ * engine 0x150c in an order ../z9-qemu's admission rules, written for the
+ * Z 9, refuse:
+ *
+ *   - it resets the units (0x150c0014 = 0xc7ff7f, 0x150c0000/04 =
+ *     0x17ff7f, 0x150c0014 = 0x4f04f; sub_40C1FD70..) while live view is
+ *     still running. The model admitted that only with the source timing
+ *     stopped. A reset needs no quiescence: here it is admitted live;
+ *   - it then stops the live-view units (0x150c000c = 0x304f, kick 0x787d)
+ *     and the direct units (0x10, 0x100 .. 0x800), now idle. Stopping an
+ *     idle unit completes at once (the model's idle-stop rule, without its
+ *     timing conditions);
+ *   - it commits and enables the still units 0x401e (upper 2, E 4, 0x150d
+ *     8, 19BC 0x10, D980 0x4000) while 19BC's direct-stop cause is still
+ *     pending: this image never acknowledges that cause (it is not in its
+ *     +0x200 mask). The unit may start again; its old cause keeps no claim
+ *     on the new latch;
+ *   - the front then asks for the still frame -- channel 0 mode 2 -> 3,
+ *     source bitmap 0x200 -- with the frame timing still running, where the
+ *     Z 9 had stopped it. ../z9-qemu's single-frame input
+ *     (primary-d980-single-frame-model) makes its one frame there anyway,
+ *     and the periodic D980 path stays quiet, so the still's data is
+ *     written once, at that request. Each still re-arms the writer's done
+ *     status (group1 bit 26), which this image never acknowledges.
+ *     With the frame, the upper unit's frame ends: +0x204 bit 6, which the
+ *     0x106 ISR's callback sub_40CAE2EC passes to the front end as
+ *     0x41D0005 (the upper unit's +0x14 bit 0 is clear for this job).
+ *
+ * DECLARED: when the still frame arrives and that its frame end comes with
+ * it. The edits are in import_z9lab.py (section 8) and nikon-z9-d980.h.
+ */
+
 Object *z63_z9lab_new(Object *owner, DeviceState *gic, uint64_t ram_size,
                       MemoryRegion *dram, MemoryRegion *buffer_ext,
                       const char *props, Error **errp);
