+/*
+ * z63-miss-log=on: name the writes the models decline. A declined write
+ * falls through to the board's own window, which stores it and says
+ * nothing -- so a model refusing a start (its admission rules) and a
+ * register no model covers look the same from outside. Each address is
+ * named for its first four distinct values, the PC with it; a declined
+ * write to engine 0x150c's control words also prints the model's admission
+ * state (active/latched/stop/reset), which is what decides. A debugging
+ * aid; off by default.
